  "correct": "C",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Write the first few signed terms",
      "body": "<p>Evaluate the sine numerator at consecutive integer indices and include the denominator in each term.</p>",
      "recap": "Moving a sine input by a half-turn changes its sign.",
      "pitfall": "The summation starts at n=0, so the first denominator is one.",
      "pause": "Write enough terms to identify the pattern, including every sign.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l15",
          "reminder": "Moving a sine input by a half-turn changes its sign."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check the ratio before using a sum",
      "body": "<p>Divide consecutive complete terms. If the ratio is constant, check its absolute value before using the infinite geometric sum.</p>",
      "recap": "A convergent geometric series has sum first term divided by one minus its signed ratio.",
      "pitfall": "Using the magnitude instead of the signed ratio changes the sum.",
      "pause": "Derive the first term and signed ratio, then calculate and simplify the sum.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l09",
          "reminder": "A convergent geometric series has sum first term divided by one minus its signed ratio."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1. Use the half-turn shift.</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>n</mi></msup><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> for every integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2. Read the geometric progression.</strong> The terms are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>&#x02026;</mi></mrow></math>, with first term <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> and ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. The absolute ratio is less than one.</p><p><strong>3. Sum.</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. <strong>Answer C.</strong></p>",
